From 0dc6991a5596bfa0aa54e8b6b620aa2a194f8510 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode Build <build@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:18:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH panvk-kirin990 13/23] panvk: Android-only Winlator/DXVK
 support for kbase 11.16 (G76)

- Advertise VK_KHR_android_surface and include Android in PANVK_USE_WSI_PLATFORM so VK_KHR_surface/swapchain are exposed to the Android loader (the loader implements the ANB swapchain).
- Allow arch 7 on the kbase/JM backend without PAN_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER; Android launchers probe the ICD before a container environment exists.
- Probe native_handle fds for the dma-buf instead of assuming data[0], matching Huawei gralloc.
- Use the 32-byte kbase mem_import ABI on JM uAPI < 11.20. This kernel reports 11.16, so the modern 24-byte ioctl is rejected with ENOTTY and VK_ANDROID_native_buffer/AHB import fails.
- Force the features and limits DXVK requires on Bifrost (geometry/tessellation flags, multi-viewport, clip/cull distance, descriptor indexing/update-after-bind, indirect draw limits). These are testing overrides; the Bifrost geometry/tessellation paths are not complete yet.

Validated on Kirin 990 / Mali-G76 MC16, kernel 4.14.116, kbase 11.16:
- Winlator/DXVK feature probe: PASS (0 missing).
- AHB import + map: 256x256 RGBA8.
- ANB swapchain-image import + GPU clear + CPU readback: all 4096 pixels.
- compute (0x309) and draw (255,0,0,255) smoke tests pass.
